/**
 * The Lexicon Lab browser engine, tested against real computation only.
 *
 * No mocks and no fixtures of convenience. In particular:
 *
 *   * the Dolch lists are compared WORD FOR WORD against the Python module that is the
 *     source of truth (`lex/dolch.py`), parsed out of the file itself — so "the TS
 *     mirrors Python" is measured, not asserted;
 *   * the Jacobi eigensolver is checked against eigenvalues computed by numpy/LAPACK
 *     (`numpy.linalg.eigvalsh`) for symmetric integer matrices generated by a Lehmer LCG
 *     that is exactly reproducible in both languages — every intermediate is an integer
 *     below 2^53, so the two languages see byte-identical inputs;
 *   * training really trains, on the real committed corpus, and the loss is measured
 *     before and after;
 *   * generation is checked for out-of-budget words at every Dolch budget size.
 */

